rs place the race in Safe or Solid Democratic territory, with Cook, Fox News, and Sabato's Crystal Ball calling it Likely Democratic. Prediction markets put Costa's chances around 95 to 96 percent.\n\nCosta has raised about $1.3 million and holds roughly $939,000 on hand, while Republican Kyle Kirkland has raised about $339,000 with under $20,000 remaining. Costa has also drawn cross-party backing, including a U.S. Chamber of Commerce endorsement, and has campaigned on water, agriculture, and rural issues that resonate locally. Kirkland, a businessman focused on farming and water policy, faces an uphill climb against a well-funded, entrenched incumbent in a favorable Democratic environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9726, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.957, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9737, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9821, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9693, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9851, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9724, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9732, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9813, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9768, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9729, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.981, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9751, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9807, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9785, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.